Looking at the current code, I need to apply double buffering to overlap the load and compute phases. The key insight is that the LU decomposition requires the full A matrix to be loaded before computation begins (due to cross-row dependencies), so double buffering applies best to the load-tile phase (overlapping tile loads) and the store-tile phase.

However, for the LU decomposition which needs all of A_local, the most meaningful double buffering is in the load tiles loop (overlapping loading tile k+1 while copying tile k into A_local) and the store tiles loop.

```cpp
